   "start": 41.6192,
   "end": 228.227,
   "text": "What nearly stopped it, and what the buyer got, the 9 separate flats would never have given him including a stamp duty difference of around 159 ,000. If you own flats that cost more to run every year, or you're trying to find a whole building and the portals only show you single units, this deal is worth watching to the end. I'm Jake, the founder of Calibre Acquire, based in London, I've been in property for 14 years and last year we transacted on over 30 million. I help investors get out of underperforming property assets and into ones that work harder for them. Fabian House is on Cannon Street Road in E1. It's free hold. There are two shops on the ground floor and the basement and nine flats above, seven two -bedroom and three two -bedrooms. There are two shops on the ground floor, a basement and nine flats above, seven two -bedroom There are two shops on the ground floor, a basement, and nine flats above, seven two -bedroom and two three -bedroom. The Sellers family built it. The site used to be a warehouse they used in the fashion trade. They knocked it down and put up the block. As far as I know, he's now retired. It was sold with the tenants in place. The rent at the time was 196 ,800 a year. It came from a letter, apart from a derelict pub in Shadwell, the site of this business, it was the first big sale to come out of a letter campaign. It was marketed at 5 million, the price agreed was 4 .775 million and it didn't move between offer and completion. On the rent at the time, that's a gross yield of about 4 .1%. For a lot of investors, 4 .1 % in East London sounds low, so why would anyone pay it? Because the rent wasn't the full rent. Let at market levels, the building could produce $278 ,400 a year. That's $81 ,600 more than it was earning. At the price paid, the yield on that full rent is about 5 .8%. Think of it like a salary that hasn't had a pay rise in years. The job is the same and the pay catches up when the contracts are renewed. The buyer is paying for the building as is with the gap built in. Split across the flats the price works out at $530 ,000 per flat and that's before you count the two shops and the basement. If you're thinking about buying or selling a property we've built a valuation report that does the work for you. We put the details in and you'll have a full report in a few minutes. It took us hours to build and we normally charge \u00a3190 for it, use the code socials and it's free. It's at www .calibreacquire .co .uk forward slash valuation dash promotion. The buyer was a private landlord who already owns several blocks in the area. For him, it was one more building on streets he already knows. He's holding it, we took over the management and the rent",
